  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Gender-based Violence Prevention and Response Services focusing on survivors of GBV in Deynille District.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltp style=&quot;&quot; class=&quot;&quot;gtThe aim of this project is to enhance the response to gender-based violence (GBV) in the Daynille&#xa0;District. This will be achieved through various interventions, such as the provision of clinical management of rape services, distribution of dignity kits, and legal aid services. The project also seeks to provide information for GBV survivors and support specialized case management, psychosocial support, and counselling through existing GBV one-stop centres and women and girls&#x2019; safe spaces.lt/pgtltp style=&quot;&quot; class=&quot;&quot;gtltbrgtFurthermore, the project intends to offer support for cash and voucher assistance through case management systems and conditional cash transfers, based on standard GBV criteria, to individual vulnerable women and girls. To promote the availability of services and prevention and mitigation of GBV, the project will also carry out awareness-raising and outreach activities.lt/pgtltp style=&quot;&quot; class=&quot;&quot;gtltbrgtlt/pgtltp style=&quot;&quot; class=&quot;&quot;gtltbrgtThe project seeks to scale up GBV intervention and provide comprehensive support to women and girls affected by GBV. By addressing the physical, emotional, legal, and economic consequences of GBV, the project aims to empower survivors and promote their overall well-being. Through a collaborative approach with key stakeholders and communities, the project intends to strengthen the capacity and coordination of GBV response in the Daynille District.ltbrgtlt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
